problem:
Given the function $f\left(x\right)=x^{m}-\dfrac{2}{x}$, and $f\left(4\right)=\dfrac{7}{2}$.
(1) Find the value of $m$;
(2) Determine the parity of $f\left(x\right)$;
(3) Determine the monotonicity of $f\left(x\right)$ on $\left(0,+\infty \right)$, and provide a proof.

